# YUMI: bowden backlash take-up -- LIVE reconfigure on a DRAINED queue.
# Variant of backlash_live_reconfig.test: the SET_PRESSURE_ADVANCE lands when
# the toolhead queue is EMPTY and fully generated (M400 just returned), with
# the offset still at -play from a retract. The return-to-zero flip is then
# stamped at the queue end with a window entirely BEHIND the flush head: no
# move can carry the ramp, it is never generated, commanded_pos stays at
# -play, and the reset wipes the model's memory of it -> the next extruding
# move jumps by the whole play -> "Invalid sequence".
# Investigation of 2026-08-14 (inject: the crash needs the conjunction of a
# live reconfigure AND a flip near in time -- traced to this drained-queue
# corner of _apply_backlash).
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG backlash_layer_change.cfg

G28
G1 X20 Y20 Z1 F6000
M83
# Exact config of the live crash (first line applied long before the print)
SET_PRESSURE_ADVANCE ADVANCE=0 SMOOTH_TIME=0 LEAD_TIME=0 BOWDEN_LENGTH=800 BACKLASH_COEF=1 BACKLASH_SPEED=40 BACKLASH_ACCEL=15000 BACKLASH_DEDUCT=0.5 BACKLASH_BLEED=10
# Settle into forward extrusion, then a retraction: offset now at -play
G1 X30 E2 F3000
G1 E-1 F6000
# DRAIN the queue: every move executed AND generated, nothing left to carry
# a ramp. M400 alone is NOT enough: print_time still sits at the retract's
# end, so the return flip's window would overlap the retract move itself and
# ride it (generated, no hole). The G4 dwell detaches print_time from the
# last move -- this is the state after an idle pause / M109 / end of print.
M400
G4 P2000
# LIVE reconfigure with the offset still pending, play and ramp GROW
# (play 1.571 -> 2.356 mm, ramp 58.9 -> 88.4 ms).
SET_PRESSURE_ADVANCE BACKLASH_COEF=1.5
# First extrusion after the reconfigure: on the buggy order the model says
# offset 0 while commanded_pos is still -play -> jump of the whole play.
G1 X40 E2 F3000
M400
